    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d709">

                <pb facs="0992" n="876" sameAs="frus:frus1923v01/pg876"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">800.51 W 89 Czechoslovakia/19: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Czechoslovakia</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Einstein</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Prague</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1923-02-19T17:00:00+01:00"><hi rendition="#italic">February 19,
                                1923—5 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 3:45 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>4. Personal letter from Dr. Beneš received today regarding the debt, etc.,
                    informs me that “in order to fix the terms of payment definitely the
                    Czecho-Slovak Government intends to send a commission <pb facs="0993" n="877"
                        xml:id="pg877"/> to the United States to negotiate the matter. The delay so
                    far was caused only by the absolute lack of the premises needed in that case.”
                    He states, “nothing lies farther from Czechoslovakia than the intention to evade
                    any of her monetary obligations.”</p>
                <p>Writing.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Einstein</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
